.SH hee-reset-tooling(1)
.PP
hee-reset-tooling \[en] real, conservative \[lq]reset to new\[rq] for
stray tool directories (real trigger, Spencer 2026-08-24:
fleet-ops#260\[cq]s stray \[ti]/tooling/bin/ cleanup, formalized into a
reusable tool instead of a one-off manual pass).
.PP
Real safety, per Spencer\[cq]s explicit call: - Dry-run by default.
Nothing is ever removed without \[en]yes \[en] an OPER must actually
agree, not just invoke the command.
- \[en]unattended (cron-shaped invocation) additionally requires the
real environment to be idle first (see is_idle below) \[en] refuses to
run destructive cleanup while a real user might be mid-work, checks
who\[cq]s actually logged in and how long they\[cq]ve been idle, not
just \[lq]no tty attached.\[rq] - NEVER touches: \[ti]/.ssh,
\[ti]/.gnupg, \[ti]/.hee/secrets, \[ti]/.config, or anything under
\[ti]/git/ \[en] refuses outright if a stray path resolves inside one of
those.
- A stray file is only removed if it\[cq]s byte-identical to the real
tracked equivalent; anything that differs, or has no tracked equivalent,
gets backed up first, never silently destroyed.
.PP
Usage: hee-reset-tooling [\[en]yes] [\[en]unattended] [\[en]idle-mins N]
.PD 0
.P
.PD
[\[en]canonical DIR] [\[en]stray DIR \&...]
(defaults: canonical = \[ti]/git/human-execution-engine/tooling/bin,
stray = \[ti]/tooling/bin \[ti]/bin, idle-mins = 10)
.PP
\f[I](no \[en]help/-h output \[en] generated from the script\[cq]s own
header comment)\f[R]
